      "id": "SNV-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "One depth for every higher-level character",
      "anchor": "inputs-stickelberger-nonvanishing",
      "statement": "For any prime ℓ, f coprime to ℓ and odd c>1 coprime to fℓ, there is d≥2 such that for every n≥d, field k of characteristic ℓ, and χ:(ℤ/fℓⁿℤ)×→k× with χ(−1)=−1, the reduction of Θ weighted by χ and pushed to Q_d is nonzero. Here Q_d=(ℤ/ℓᵈℤ)×/red(W), W=μ_{φ(ℓ^e)}(ℤℓ), with e=1 for odd ℓ and e=2 for ℓ=2.",
      "hypotheses": "The original theorem takes a divisibility witness ℓᵈ∣fℓⁿ, available for n≥d. Nonvanishing as a group-ring element says at least one quotient coefficient is nonzero. A common nonzero coefficient across all χ or n is not asserted. The cyclotomic application takes f>1 and c=2fℓ+1.",
