      "title": "A character-weighted finite difference with a unit coefficient",
      "anchor": "inputs-stickelberger-difference",
      "statement": "Set B=cfℓ. If the twisted projection were zero, the pushforward α(y)=Σ_{s↦y} g(s)Ψ(s), where Ψ is χ extended by zero on nonunits, would satisfy Σ_{r∈R} α(r⁻¹y)=0. Its translation by B satisfies α(y)−α(y−B)=Σ_{0≤j<B, j≡y (mod ℓᵈ)}P(j), with P(j)=Ψ(j)(1−c·1_{c|j}) and P(1)=1.",
      "hypotheses": "Above assumptions; R consists of one representative of each pair {r,−r} in W, and reduction is faithful on W for d≥2. Characteristic ℓ and the field hypothesis ensure χ kills ℓ-power order units.",
      "definitions": [
        "sum over an additive reduction fibre",
        "invariance under change of sign",
        "period fℓ",
        "finite difference of the centered floor"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-stickelberger-pulse"
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
