      "id": "SNV-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Sinnott separation of finitely many translation exponents",
      "anchor": "inputs-stickelberger-sinnott",
      "statement": "For finitely many nonempty, pairwise rationally noncollinear ℓ-adic unit directions R and B>0, a depth uniform in the coefficient ring, forcing terms P and function α makes the hypothesized average-zero and difference equations imply all P(j)=0 for 0≤j<B. This contradicts the chosen P(1)=1.",
      "hypotheses": "The abstract finite-depth theorem works over any commutative coefficient ring. It requires a fixed finite nonempty family with ar=bu for distinct r,u and integers a,b only when a=0. The chosen directions from W meet this by their finite order and choice up to sign.",
      "definitions": [
        "translation group algebra",
        "support separated modulo ℓᵈ",
        "quotient by ℤ·Br₀",
        "injectivity of a difference in an infinite-order direction"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-stickelberger-separation"
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
      "correspondence": "Put A_r=Σ_yα(y)X^{ry}, P_r=Σ_jP(j)X^{jr}. The finite equality P_r=(1−X^{Br})A_r and Σ A_r=0 give Σ_r P_r Π_{u≠r}(1−X^{Bu})=0. Its possible exponents depend only on R and B. At a common separating depth the equality lifts to k[ℤℓ] for the additive group. Taking exponents modulo the algebraic subgroup ℤ·Br₀ kills all other summands. Each remaining translation by Bu has infinite order in that quotient and repeated equality of a coefficient is incompatible with finite nonempty support. After cancellation, 0≤j<B are distinct on the r₀ direction.",
